From 3314eb1a18cbf5f9f8f7ad9ad971f0bef4f04623 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 13:43:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(tts): add Fish Audio TTS provider, locked to the free
 S2.1 Pro tier by default
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

pipecat already ships a Fish Audio TTS service (FishAudioTTSService,
WebSocket streaming over ormsgpack) but dograh never wired it into the
service configuration, so Fish Audio could not be selected as a Voice
provider in the cascading pipeline.

Wire it through:
- registry: ServiceProviders.FISH + FishTTSConfiguration (model, voice
  reference ID, latency, speed, volume, normalize) registered in
  TTSConfig. The default and only advertised model is s2.1-pro-free,
  the free-of-charge tier of S2.1 Pro served under Fish Audio's Fair
  Use policy.
- paid-model gate: every other Fish model is treated as paid and is
  rejected — at configuration save (pydantic field validator) and again
  at service creation (factory) — unless the operator explicitly sets
  ALLOW_PAID_FISH_MODELS=true on the API server (default false). A
  rejected paid selection fails with a 400; it never falls back to
  another model, and the free tier never silently escalates to a paid
  one: reconnect attempts after rate limiting or free-model
  unavailability always request the configured free model (test-proven
  against the real service's reconnect path). The schema advertises
  only the free model, so the UI dropdown shows no paid options.
- service_factory: build FishAudioTTSService in create_tts_service.
  PCM output; sample rate resolves from the pipeline StartFrame like
  other providers, so both 8 kHz telephony and 16 kHz WebRTC work. An
  empty voice stays unset so no empty reference_id reaches the wire.
- check_validity: validate the key against the wallet credit endpoint;
  only a clear auth failure rejects save.
- Dockerfile + setup_requirements.sh: install pipecat's fish extra
  (ormsgpack).
- openapi.json regenerated via scripts.dump_docs_openapi; ui client
  types regenerated; docs updated; 21 factory/gate/validation tests.

